/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# IDE
/.idea/

# Build artifacts from xtask (SBOM, DST reports)
/artifacts/

# Key material and certificates — never in the tree.
#
# The rule is broad, and it means it: the risk is not the files that lie here
# today — those one knows —, but the next one somebody drops while trying
# something out. A private key in the repository is an incident even when it
# was "only test stuff": the history does not forget, and cutting it out
# afterwards means pulling every clone anew.
#
# Should a certificate ever really belong checked in — a trust anchor as a
# test fixture, say —, that is a deliberate act: `git add -f <file>`. Exactly
# that deliberateness is the rule's purpose.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# Python bytecode of the dossier generator (plans/dossier.py).
__pycache__/
